      "message": "Stack the on-farm times and write them in full\n\nJames asked for each on-farm \"Pickup time\" radio on its own line,\nlabeled with both ends and their minutes (#616): \"8:00 – 10:00 AM\",\n\"10:00 AM – 12:00 PM\". AM or PM is written once when the ends share\nit, and twelve o'clock is \"12:00 PM\", never \"noon\".\n\nfullWindowLabel in lib/schedule.mjs writes the label from a window's\nfrom and to. windowLabel (\"9 AM – noon\") is left as it is: emails,\norder cards and Square notes read it. The value each radio sends,\nthe window's id, does not change.\n\nThe radios stack at every width (.order-radios-stack; the contact\nradios, which share .order-radios, stay in a row). Each label sits\nin one text-nowrap span, set by setWhole in keep-together.mjs, since\nkeepTogether would let a label break at its dash. No no-break space\nis written.\n\nThe same labels go where else a customer picks an on-farm time: the\nlapsed dialog's times, after the day, and the account's Change\npickup, whose times stack too. Change pickup's \"(as booked)\" time\nstays on windowLabel, as the order card reads.",
